# Applets that CANNOT be built on NeoOS today, and why.
#
# Each needs a Linux kernel facility that does not exist here, and
# musl deliberately does not ship Linux kernel headers -- so these fail
# at COMPILE time, deep inside busybox, with an error nowhere near the
# option that caused it. Listing them here turns that into an immediate
# refusal naming the option.
#
# This is not a permanent list. The network milestone (PCI -> NIC ->
# Ethernet/ARP -> ICMP -> TCP) is what makes most of it buildable; the
# entry says what each is waiting for.

CONFIG_IP          netlink (linux/netlink.h, if_arp.h, asm/types.h)
CONFIG_TC          netlink, and traffic control NeoOS has no concept of
CONFIG_IFCONFIG    linux/if.h and SIOCGIFCONF ioctls on a real interface
CONFIG_ROUTE       kernel routing table ioctls
CONFIG_NETSTAT     /proc/net/*, which NeoOS's procfs does not provide
CONFIG_PING        raw sockets (SOCK_RAW) and ICMP
CONFIG_UDHCPC      linux/filter.h (BPF) and raw sockets
CONFIG_UDHCPD      linux/filter.h (BPF) and raw sockets
CONFIG_ARPING      raw sockets
CONFIG_BRCTL       bridge ioctls
CONFIG_TRACEROUTE  raw sockets
CONFIG_FREE        sysinfo(2), which NeoOS has no syscall for
CONFIG_UPTIME      sysinfo(2), which NeoOS has no syscall for
